%% Per-pod store — Packaging & Distributing Your App, lab exercise 5 (collapsible "Why one replica").
%% The notifications service keeps its store in each pod's memory. With two replicas behind one
%% Service, the test's POST can land on one pod and its GET on the other, which never saw the write;
%% that is why the upgrade scales back to one replica before `helm test`.
%% Shape (diagram-size-guard): LR, longest chain 3, no subgraph, labels at most 2 lines.
flowchart LR
  T["test Pod<br/>POST, then GET"] --> S["Service<br/>two replicas"]
  S -->|"POST"| A["pod A<br/>holds CLM-TEST"]
  S -.->|"GET"| B["pod B<br/>never saw the write"]
  classDef act fill:#e8eaf6,stroke:#3949ab,color:#1a237e;
  classDef good fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  classDef bad fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#a50e0e;
  class T,S act; class A good; class B bad;
